{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals","id":1352992,"title":"The Hantu: Another group of Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-06T06:07:03-08:00","id":1352992,"title":"The Hantu: Another group of Supernaturals","content":"I learned a new word today, Hantu. Hantu seems to be a Maylay word covering ghosts, vampires, and fairy-like spirits. Later today I'll post links to any Hantu lore I find on the nets. Maybe we can make up exotic new changelings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:11:49-08:00","id":1353085,"title":"","content":"Well here's a link to the Wikipedia article <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hantu_(supernatural_creature)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hantu_...ural_creature)</a>. It seems that the term Anito comes closer to our western take on the Fairies, here's a link <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anito\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anito</a> . I'll try to do some web surfing to see if any gameable info on these creatures is available. At this point it looks like the Hantu are the Malay equivalent to the Thallain and the Anito are Malay Changlings and/or Fay. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have better data?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-06-2019, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T14:55:19-08:00","id":1354929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals?p=1353085#post1353085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well here's a link to the Wikipedia article <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hantu_(supernatural_creature)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hantu_...ural_creature)</a>. It seems that the term Anito comes closer to our western take on the Fairies, here's a link <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anito\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anito</a> . I'll try to do some web surfing to see if any gameable info on these creatures is available. At this point it looks like the Hantu are the Malay equivalent to the Thallain and the Anito are Malay Changlings and/or Fay.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have better data?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just be aware that Hantu ( Inonesian and Malaysian word) is a very, very broad term that covers everything from ghosts to demons to ' evil spirits' to 'faeries' and is even stretched to include Naga and cryptids on occasion.<br /> <br /> Heres some fun Hantu from Borneo: <a href=\"https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&amp;sl=id&amp;u=https://www.boombastis.com/hantu-kalimantan/84176&amp;prev=search\" target=\"_blank\">https://translate.google.com/transla...76&amp;prev=search</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T15:02:16-08:00","id":1354930,"title":"","content":"Probably the closest you get to 'faeries' are beings like Orang Bunian, but others such as Orang Pendek, Orang Bati ( depending on the description given), Ebu Gogo or even Genderuwa could work as fae beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T04:35:01-08:00","id":1354979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals?p=1354930#post1354930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the closest you get to 'faeries' are beings like Orang Bunian, but others such as Orang Pendek, Orang Bati ( depending on the description given), Ebu Gogo or even Genderuwa could work as fae beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But it is nice to have options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T09:28:54-08:00","id":1355019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals?p=1354930#post1354930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the closest you get to 'faeries' are beings like Orang Bunian, but others such as Orang Pendek, Orang Bati ( depending on the description given), Ebu Gogo or even Genderuwa could work as fae beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be neat if such fae were connected to the Homo floresiensis hominids. Perhaps the dreaming memory of those ancient folk and their contact with ancient humans.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would treat such fae as being more like the Nunnehi or Menehune, being nature oriented types of fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 12-15-2019, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T13:48:18-08:00","id":1355045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals?p=1355019#post1355019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be neat if such fae were connected to the Homo floresiensis hominids. Perhaps the dreaming memory of those ancient folk and their contact with ancient humans.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would treat such fae as being more like the Nunnehi or Menehune, being nature oriented types of fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though Orang Bunian stories could drop almost seamlessly into a book of western Fairy Tales, they're basically 'elves.<br /> <br /> The others are definitely a touch more primal.<br /> <br /> I set most of my campaigns in SE Asia and Oceania so have a bunch more links if you want them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T13:50:25-08:00","id":1355047,"title":"","content":"Ebu Gogo are pretty much straight up folk memories of Homo floresiensis remains and artifacts....the others, not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:43:03-08:00","id":1355093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1352992-the-hantu-another-group-of-supernaturals?p=1355045#post1355045\" rel=